{title: 457 - I Love to Tell the Story}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #457 • HANKEY • 7.6.7.6.D.}
{lyricist: Katherine Hankey}
{composer: William G. Fischer}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 457}
{meta: tune HANKEY}
{meta: meter 7.6.7.6.D.}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]I love to tell the story
[G/B]Of [C]unseen things above,
[G]Of [D]Jesus and [G/D]His glory,
[G]Of Jesus and His love.
[D]I love to [D7]tell the [G]story,
[G]Because [Em]I know ’tis true;
[Bm]It [C]satisfies my longings
[G]As [D7]nothing [G/D]else [D7]can [G]do.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[G]I [D]love to [D7]tell the [G]story,
[G/B]'twill [C]be my theme in glory,
[G]to tell the old, old story
[C]of [G/D]Jesus [D7]and [G]his love.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]I love to tell the story;
[G/B]more [C]wonderful it seems
[G]than [D]all the golden [G]fancies
[G]of all our golden dreams.
[D]I love to [D7]tell the [G]story,
[G]it [Em]did so much for me;
[Bm]and [C]that is just the reason
[G]I [D7]tell it [G/D]now [D7]to [G]thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]I love to tell the story;
[G/B]'tis [C]pleasant to repeat
[G]what [D]seems, each time [G/D]I tell it,
[G]more wonderfully sweet.
[D]I love to [D7]tell the [G]story,
[G]for [Em]some have never heard
[Bm]the [C]message of salvation
[G]from [D7]God's own [G/D]holy Word.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]I love to tell the story,
[G/B]for [C]those who know it best
[G]seem [D]hungering [G/D]and thirsting
[G]to hear it like the rest.
[D]And when, in scenes [D7]of [G]glory,
[G]I [Em]sing the new, new song,
[Bm]'twill [C]be the old, old story
[G]that [D7]I have [G/D]loved [D7]so [G]long.
{end_of_verse}
